    "line": 44,
    "summary": "The `web` job only ever builds and pushes `:latest`/`:<sha>` (baked with the local-dev `VITE_API_BASE_URL`); the NAS-targeted `:nas` image (baked with the NAS's LAN API URL) was built and pushed by hand during R-5, and R-9's own log confirms CI still doesn't touch it — a pure SPA change (R-9 itself) shipped code that `docker compose pull` on the NAS silently did not receive until someone remembered to rebuild `:nas` manually.",
    "failure_scenario": "The NAS deploy target is a manual, undocumented-in-CI special case bolted onto an otherwise general publish mechanism (build once, tag twice). The next SPA change (or the next deploy target anyone adds — a staging env, a second customer's LAN box) needs its own remembered manual `docker build --build-arg VITE_API_BASE_URL=...` step, with nothing in CI to catch a forgotten one. The general fix is a second matrix/job in this workflow keyed by target (env: local/nas/...) that bakes `VITE_API_BASE_URL` per target and pushes both tags on every push, so 'which image is actually running on the NAS' is never a question only a human's memory can answer."
  },
  {
    "file": "docker/entrypoint.sh",
    "line": 22,
    "summary": "R-6's entrypoint.sh re-implements, in POSIX sh, the exact `sqlite:///` prefix-stripping logic that `scripts/seed.py`'s `_reset_database_file` (scripts/seed.py:69-83) already has in Python, so it can decide whether to auto-seed.",
    "failure_scenario": "Two independent implementations of 'how to turn MISSION_CONTROL_DATABASE_URL into a filesystem path' now have to be kept in sync by hand across a language boundary (Python vs. sh); the shell copy is exercised only by container startup, not by the Python test suite (137 tests never touch it). The next change to the URL scheme (e.g. supporting a non-default path convention, or a second sqlite variant) is likely to update seed.py and silently miss entrypoint.sh, reintroducing the exact 'restart wipes your data' bug R-6 was written to prevent. A general fix: have seed.py expose a small `resolve_sqlite_path(url) -> str | None` (or a `--db-exists` CLI check) that entrypoint.sh shells out to, so there is one implementation, not two hand-synced ones."
  },
  {
    "file": "scripts/seed.py",
    "line": 99,
    "summary": "R-8's final pass keeps `_demo_password(email)` taking an `email` parameter it now explicitly discards (`del email`), justified in the docstring only as 'kept as the extension point if a future need... brings back a derived password.'",
    "failure_scenario": "Minor, but it's a speculative seam kept for a hypothetical future special case (per-user secrecy) rather than removed and re-added if that need actually arrives — the kind of premature generality that tends to accrete: the next person touching this file inherits an unused parameter and has to figure out whether it's load-bearing. Low risk here (contained to one seed script, no shared infra), so this is a nice-to-simplify rather than a fragility, but worth a one-line note; the cleaner fix is to drop the parameter now and let a real future requirement decide the API shape then."
  }
]

